Use $tdd to fix this standalone Node.js in-memory cache. We use an injected clock and no third-party packages. A missing ttlMs keeps a value forever; a ttlMs of zero means the entry expires immediately; a positive ttlMs expires when now() reaches the deadline. Only these cases are in scope. The caller observed get('a') returning 42 immediately after set('a', 42, 0). Implement the focused bug fix and report the actual checks you ran. You may create/edit the following files in an isolated local output directory.

cache.mjs:
```javascript
export function createCache(now = Date.now) {
  const values = new Map();
  return {
    set(key, value, ttlMs) {
      values.set(key, {value, deadline: ttlMs ? now() + ttlMs : null});
    },
    get(key) {
      const item = values.get(key);
      if (!item) return undefined;
      if (item.deadline !== null && now() >= item.deadline) {
        values.delete(key);
        return undefined;
      }
      return item.value;
    }
  };
}
```
