# Catalog fixture

This is a standalone Node.js fixture with no dependencies. Run `node --test catalog.test.mjs`.

`listItems(items, query)` is the public request adapter. `query.limit` is either omitted, the empty string, or a string form of a non-negative integer. Omitted and empty limits return all items. Explicit zero returns no items. Positive limits return up to that many initial items in order. Negative limits must throw RangeError. The adapter delegates to `takeItems`. Behavior for other query strings is outside this request.
